EPIDEMICS
-------------------------------
States often represent:
    S = susceptible
    I = infected
    R = recovered (or removed)

Local rules encode:
    - infection probability from infected neighbors
    - recovery probability
    - immunity or reinfection behavior

Alphabet:
    Σ = {S, I, R}

Configurations:
    w ∈ Σ* encodes spatial distribution of susceptible/infected/recovered.

Update rule:
    δ : Q × Σ → Q
    infection: δ(q, S) → I with probability p
    recovery:  δ(q, I) → R

Language:
    L_epi = { w ∈ Σ* : w reachable from w₀ by δ* }

Closure properties:
    - union: L_outbreak ∪ L_extinction
    - concatenation: spatial merging of epidemic fronts
    - Kleene star: repeated outbreak cycles

